WEBVTT

00:00:00.230 --> 00:00:04.190
In this place so unreal

00:00:03.860 --> 00:00:07.820
I wait for dawn to come

00:00:07.490 --> 00:00:12.950
Farther and farther, like the sky I saw that day

00:00:15.120 --> 00:00:19.210
What a joke this hope is

00:00:18.920 --> 00:00:22.750
I acted as if I had forgotten

00:00:22.500 --> 00:00:28.260
Farther and farther, like the dream I saw that day

00:00:29.470 --> 00:00:34.140
I just want to know the meaning of it

00:00:33.680 --> 00:00:37.310
Within this scattered time

00:00:37.020 --> 00:00:41.100
Along with the breath of ours

00:00:41.150 --> 00:00:45.070
And of this pain that never goes away

00:00:44.770 --> 00:00:48.610
Even though the roaring of the sea muffles the voices

00:00:48.490 --> 00:00:52.490
Darkness engulfs everything ahead

00:00:52.200 --> 00:00:56.540
The light that passes through our fragile hearts

00:00:56.410 --> 00:00:59.960
Won't go away

00:00:59.750 --> 00:01:03.750
We only relied on our compass

00:01:03.460 --> 00:01:07.920
We believed you

00:01:07.670 --> 00:01:14.760
While we stand here

00:01:14.470 --> 00:01:19.890
We're searching for the unseen future

00:01:22.900 --> 00:01:29.860
Zipang

00:01:31.820 --> 00:01:33.990
At the beginning of the 21st Century,

00:01:34.150 --> 00:01:38.110
the SDF Navy's newest AEGIS class vessel, Mirai,

00:01:38.110 --> 00:01:40.580
sets off from the Yokosuka Base.

00:01:42.450 --> 00:01:45.000
However, just as they entered the Pacific Ocean,

00:01:45.000 --> 00:01:48.000
Mirai was faced with abnormal atmospheric conditions.

00:01:49.500 --> 00:01:52.460
She was then thrown back to 1942, June 4th,

00:01:52.460 --> 00:01:54.840
into the Battle of Midway.

00:01:55.800 --> 00:01:58.680
Caught in the midst of an ongoing war,

00:01:58.680 --> 00:02:05.060
what should the 241 SDF members of the Mirai do in this era?

00:02:05.270 --> 00:02:08.020
We have yet to find the answer.

00:02:13.150 --> 00:02:17.950
Kusaka's Choice

00:02:17.990 --> 00:02:21.030
When the torpedoes were about 10 meters from us,

00:02:21.030 --> 00:02:24.370
my adrenaline was pumping, and my blood flowed faster.

00:02:24.370 --> 00:02:27.540
My blood was pulsing hard, but...

00:02:27.620 --> 00:02:31.080
I was surprisingly composed. It's just like the drills.

00:02:31.080 --> 00:02:34.840
Because you're only watching the monitor inside the CIC.

00:02:34.840 --> 00:02:38.010
It doesn't feel real. We're on the wing over here.

00:02:38.010 --> 00:02:41.470
As the torpedoes drew closer, my knees started shaking.

00:02:41.640 --> 00:02:44.470
"ASROC: Anti-Submarine Rocket"

00:02:41.640 --> 00:02:44.470
I'm really surprised about the ASROC.

00:02:44.470 --> 00:02:46.430
The Torpedo Chief pressed the release button, right?

00:02:46.430 --> 00:02:48.430
The Weapons Officer must've given him a good scolding...

00:02:48.430 --> 00:02:50.100
...and made him wet his pants!

00:02:53.060 --> 00:02:55.610
He wasn't the only one who was frightened.

00:02:55.690 --> 00:02:58.440
If I was in the same position as Lieutenant Yonekura,

00:02:58.440 --> 00:03:00.610
I might've pushed the button myself too.

00:03:00.700 --> 00:03:03.990
That's right, he's not the only one who was scared.

00:03:03.990 --> 00:03:07.500
Under those circumstances, no one can remain calm.

00:03:08.200 --> 00:03:11.580
The longer we stay inside this era, the worse it'll be.

00:03:12.080 --> 00:03:15.090
What's going to happen... to all of us here?

00:03:20.010 --> 00:03:21.510
Lieutenant Satake.

00:03:21.510 --> 00:03:23.180
Oh, thank you.

00:03:23.300 --> 00:03:26.600
Right now, everyone's talking about the ASROC firing error.

00:03:26.720 --> 00:03:29.560
You can't call deliberation a human error, right?

00:03:29.560 --> 00:03:32.230
It wasn't right of him to take action without orders,

00:03:32.230 --> 00:03:35.820
but in a real battle, you can only choose to fire, or not to fire.

00:03:35.820 --> 00:03:38.820
Even for me, self-defense would be top priority.

00:03:38.820 --> 00:03:42.990
I'm counting on you. A pilot and his gunner should be one.

00:03:42.990 --> 00:03:44.950
We'll enter the war and go down together.

00:03:45.410 --> 00:03:48.330
Don't say such ominous things.

00:03:48.330 --> 00:03:51.250
A suicide together with you?

00:03:51.250 --> 00:03:53.710
I don't think I know you long enough for that.

00:03:53.710 --> 00:03:55.590
That's harsh. Well,

00:03:55.590 --> 00:03:58.000
I don't intend to lose my life for nothing...

00:03:58.000 --> 00:04:00.720
...in this unfamiliar world, either.

00:04:01.920 --> 00:04:03.720
- Lieutenant Satake...
- Yes?

00:04:04.140 --> 00:04:07.470
What if... we are stuck in this world forever?

00:04:07.470 --> 00:04:10.310
What should we be doing in this era instead?

00:04:11.770 --> 00:04:13.480
Beats me.

00:04:13.640 --> 00:04:16.810
The crew are feeling insecure after their first war encounter.

00:04:16.810 --> 00:04:18.270
We have no allies.

00:04:18.270 --> 00:04:21.650
And we face the uncertainty of not being able to go back home.

00:04:22.450 --> 00:04:25.490
From these building tensions, if another battle should break out,

00:04:25.780 --> 00:04:27.280
it'll be dangerous.

00:04:27.280 --> 00:04:29.990
Yonekura's breakdown is a good indication.

00:04:29.990 --> 00:04:31.160
That's right.

00:04:31.160 --> 00:04:34.120
We were lucky this time round, but what about the next?

00:04:34.120 --> 00:04:36.000
We have to take action now.

00:04:36.330 --> 00:04:39.300
The longer we take to decide, the fewer options we'll have.

00:04:39.300 --> 00:04:43.380
I know, but there's something I'm more worried about now.

00:04:43.510 --> 00:04:46.340
Lieutenant, did Kusaka witness everything?

00:04:46.340 --> 00:04:50.600
Yes, he insisted on watching the battle for himself on the deck.

00:04:50.770 --> 00:04:53.730
After witnessing the ASROC, did he say anything?

00:04:53.850 --> 00:04:57.060
"Is this part of God's plan? Or a will of the Devil?"

00:04:57.060 --> 00:05:00.230
And "this is a battle of the twenty-first century."

00:05:02.320 --> 00:05:05.070
We can't let him leave. He knows too much.

00:05:05.320 --> 00:05:08.070
When we examined the black leather bag he had with him,

00:05:08.070 --> 00:05:10.580
we found a black leather bound report book.

00:05:11.910 --> 00:05:16.170
A detailed account of the Battle of Midway was recorded inside.

00:05:16.170 --> 00:05:17.580
Someone carrying a thing like that must be...

00:05:18.080 --> 00:05:19.590
...an intelligence professional.

00:05:19.750 --> 00:05:21.000
I'm guessing,

00:05:21.000 --> 00:05:24.670
his plane was shot down on his way back to the main unit.

00:05:24.670 --> 00:05:27.590
To be a Lieutenant Commander at such a young age,

00:05:27.590 --> 00:05:29.350
he must be an elite soldier.

00:05:29.350 --> 00:05:31.100
A worst case scenario.

00:05:31.100 --> 00:05:35.640
If we let him be, he'll dig out every detail about this ship.

00:05:35.640 --> 00:05:38.350
If he adds on to the insecurity that's affecting the crew,

00:05:38.350 --> 00:05:40.190
the peace of this ship will not hold.

00:05:40.190 --> 00:05:43.780
So that means, in that era, Japan still exists, right?

00:05:43.780 --> 00:05:45.320
But Kikuchi,

00:05:45.530 --> 00:05:48.610
that man could help us obtain some supplies.

00:05:48.700 --> 00:05:50.580
Whether it's fuel or food,

00:05:50.580 --> 00:05:52.540
we'd want it to come from Japan, right?

00:05:52.870 --> 00:05:55.040
He'll be our handy link with the supplies.

00:05:55.040 --> 00:05:56.870
They're not going to give it to us for nothing.

00:05:56.870 --> 00:05:59.920
They'll ask to cooperate with the Imperial Japanese Military.

00:06:00.420 --> 00:06:03.800
And if that happens, we will definitely change history itself.

00:06:04.010 --> 00:06:05.670
I don't want to give up.

00:06:05.670 --> 00:06:07.430
If we change history as we please,

00:06:07.430 --> 00:06:09.800
our twenty-first century will cease to exist!

00:06:10.090 --> 00:06:12.560
Our families will also disappear then.

00:06:13.760 --> 00:06:16.230
But... it's no use after all,

00:06:16.230 --> 00:06:20.060
to try to prevent all information of this ship from leaking out.

00:06:20.560 --> 00:06:23.520
If you want to be absolutely sure, there's only one way.

00:06:24.730 --> 00:06:26.150
Lieutenant.

00:06:26.360 --> 00:06:28.450
Can I have the key to the sick bay?

00:06:28.450 --> 00:06:30.360
Oh, sure.

00:06:32.370 --> 00:06:34.040
Hey?!

00:06:34.290 --> 00:06:37.710
Like I've mentioned before, this is my responsibility.

00:06:37.710 --> 00:06:39.540
I hope all of you will not interfere with this.

00:06:51.800 --> 00:06:52.970
Where's your uniform?

00:06:53.140 --> 00:06:56.890
The medical officer sent it for cleaning, and gave me this instead.

00:06:56.890 --> 00:06:58.940
Well, how do I look?

00:06:58.980 --> 00:07:00.730
It doesn't go with the military sword.

00:07:00.980 --> 00:07:03.810
It's my walking stick now. Don't be so hard on me.

00:07:03.900 --> 00:07:06.690
So, you can walk, right? Please come along with me.

00:07:06.820 --> 00:07:09.530
I can go outside? That's wonderful.

00:07:09.530 --> 00:07:11.610
I was getting bored with nothing to do.

00:07:14.240 --> 00:07:16.490
Are you giving me a tour of this ship?

00:07:16.490 --> 00:07:17.950
Something like that.

00:07:18.450 --> 00:07:20.410
I'm grateful for your concern.

00:07:20.410 --> 00:07:22.040
It's up ahead.

00:07:23.290 --> 00:07:25.800
It's up ahead? Don't tell me...?

00:07:30.970 --> 00:07:31.930
This is...?

00:07:32.180 --> 00:07:33.800
It's the ship's library.

00:07:33.800 --> 00:07:36.220
Nothing compared to the library on land,

00:07:36.220 --> 00:07:38.180
but it's well stocked on war history.

00:07:39.770 --> 00:07:44.520
Geez, those two keep doing things to give me a heart attack.

00:07:45.150 --> 00:07:48.990
The development of this war, and Japan after the war.

00:07:48.990 --> 00:07:51.950
It's all data that should not exist in this era.

00:07:51.950 --> 00:07:55.120
Whether to read them or not, the choice is yours.

00:07:55.120 --> 00:07:57.410
Why are you showing me these things?

00:07:57.540 --> 00:08:00.910
Given the opportunity, you would want to find out, right?

00:08:01.370 --> 00:08:03.580
Because that's part of your job, isn't it?

00:08:04.130 --> 00:08:05.630
What happens after I read?

00:08:06.090 --> 00:08:07.380
Be mentally prepared.

00:08:09.510 --> 00:08:12.880
Do you mean to say I won't be leaving this ship alive, then?

00:08:12.880 --> 00:08:14.930
You have been warned. Anyway,

00:08:14.930 --> 00:08:18.470
if you read them, you will know too much about us and this ship.

00:08:18.470 --> 00:08:22.270
By then, you will have to share the same fate as us all.

00:08:22.640 --> 00:08:24.650
I'm asking you to prepare yourself for that.

00:08:26.110 --> 00:08:28.690
On the day that you rescued me,

00:08:28.690 --> 00:08:31.190
Lieutenant Commander Takumi Kusaka...

00:08:31.190 --> 00:08:32.990
...ceased to exist.

00:08:34.740 --> 00:08:36.570
That's what I wanted to hear.

00:08:37.870 --> 00:08:40.370
Mistakes of the Pacific War

00:08:42.870 --> 00:08:46.000
Aren't you afraid to know how your fate will turn out?

00:08:46.880 --> 00:08:50.500
The purpose of life... is to learn.

00:08:58.140 --> 00:09:00.350
Tomorrow at 0600,

00:09:00.350 --> 00:09:03.230
send a helicopter to Ogasawara for air observation.

00:09:03.430 --> 00:09:05.900
During the Showa 17th year, Chichijima...

00:09:05.900 --> 00:09:09.770
...should already have a well fortified naval division in place.

00:09:09.770 --> 00:09:11.650
Of course, in our Heisei period,

00:09:11.650 --> 00:09:13.900
there are patrols stationed in Chichijima.

00:09:14.110 --> 00:09:16.240
I'm sure everyone is anxious to know which Navy Division...

00:09:16.240 --> 00:09:17.780
...is currently stationed there.

00:09:19.740 --> 00:09:22.870
That's when we'll decide whether to enter Yokosuka Base.

00:09:23.200 --> 00:09:27.370
If it is Showa 17th year, it will be difficult for us to enter the base.

00:09:27.920 --> 00:09:31.460
What should we do if there are those who insist on returning?

00:09:31.710 --> 00:09:34.170
To return is to face interrogation by the army.

00:09:34.170 --> 00:09:36.930
I understand how they're feeling, but it's not a simple matter.

00:09:37.890 --> 00:09:40.600
By the way, Lieutenant Kusaka is still inside the library?

00:09:40.600 --> 00:09:43.470
Yes. It has been a day since then.

00:09:43.470 --> 00:09:44.730
He's shut himself inside.

00:09:44.730 --> 00:09:46.980
He hasn't taken any food, except for some water.

00:09:51.770 --> 00:09:54.150
Saipan, Guam, Tinian.

00:09:54.150 --> 00:09:55.650
All divisions destroyed.

00:09:56.110 --> 00:10:00.160
Deutsch Third Reich Fuhrer, Hitler, committed suicide.

00:10:00.660 --> 00:10:04.540
Battle of Okinawa, death of 100,000 civilians.

00:10:04.790 --> 00:10:07.460
Battleships Yamato and Musashi, sunk.

00:10:07.460 --> 00:10:10.580
Navy Special Division, Kamikaze Task Force, created.

00:10:10.580 --> 00:10:13.210
Manned Torpedoes, Kaiten, deployed.

00:10:13.920 --> 00:10:16.130
Air raids extended nationwide.

00:10:16.130 --> 00:10:20.010
Bombing of Tokyo, 84,000 civilians burnt to death.

00:10:20.010 --> 00:10:22.560
America completes the atomic bomb.

00:10:22.810 --> 00:10:24.890
And drops it on Hiroshima and Nagasaki.

00:10:24.890 --> 00:10:26.680
115,000 in Hiroshima,

00:10:26.680 --> 00:10:30.600
and 73.000 lives in Nagasaki were claimed by just two bombs.

00:10:27.480 --> 00:10:31.110
On 15
August
1945, Japan
accepts the
Potsdam
Proclamation
and
unconditional
surrender.

00:10:30.610 --> 00:10:34.110
Around 2
million
soldiers,
military
personnel
and civilians
were killed
in the
great war.

00:10:33.320 --> 00:10:35.480
What I had predicted was right.

00:10:35.480 --> 00:10:37.190
The clash between the Eastern Imperial Way...

00:10:37.190 --> 00:10:40.780
...and the Western Supremacy resulted in victory for the West.

00:10:45.240 --> 00:10:47.160
It's a revelation.

00:10:48.620 --> 00:10:50.830
All 32 years of my life...

00:10:51.540 --> 00:10:53.540
...is for this enlightenment.

00:10:55.800 --> 00:10:58.470
Letting him know about the history of the future...

00:10:58.470 --> 00:11:02.260
...was a right thing to do, and also a cruel one at that.

00:11:02.680 --> 00:11:04.850
Did you do that out of sympathy?

00:11:04.850 --> 00:11:07.220
Or out of jealousy, I wonder?

00:11:07.310 --> 00:11:08.810
Jealousy?

00:11:08.890 --> 00:11:10.560
In this era of his,

00:11:10.560 --> 00:11:12.860
he has a mission he needs to see through.

00:11:12.860 --> 00:11:15.570
Something which we don't have now.

00:11:16.570 --> 00:11:18.650
I don't understand.

00:11:18.650 --> 00:11:21.570
However, to continue sailing,

00:11:21.700 --> 00:11:24.280
I really wanted him to have the same mindset...

00:11:24.280 --> 00:11:26.830
...as the rest of the 241 members of this ship.

00:11:29.620 --> 00:11:32.670
This is the story of the country,

00:11:33.040 --> 00:11:35.040
as it continues into the 21st Century.

00:11:35.090 --> 00:11:38.960
That room must be a pandora's box for Lieutenant Commander Kusaka.

00:11:39.130 --> 00:11:41.680
After the hurricane of disasters,

00:11:41.840 --> 00:11:44.890
I wonder if there's any hope left for him in there?

00:11:46.220 --> 00:11:48.930
The purpose of life is to pursue knowledge.

00:11:49.390 --> 00:11:50.890
That's what he said to me.

00:11:56.690 --> 00:11:58.440
60 years...

00:11:59.150 --> 00:12:02.860
In just 60 years after the war...?

00:12:08.490 --> 00:12:11.660
Lieutenant Satake, 0600.

00:12:11.660 --> 00:12:13.710
Departing for Ogasawara now.

00:12:13.710 --> 00:12:16.590
Be on the lookout for other planes, too.

00:12:16.590 --> 00:12:19.000
We do not want our location to be disclosed.

00:12:19.000 --> 00:12:21.720
What? They're nothing but seaplanes on Geta sandals.

00:12:21.720 --> 00:12:23.800
The best they can manage is probably around 300 km<i>l</i>h.

00:12:23.880 --> 00:12:26.800
At 450 km<i>l</i>h, they'll never outrun us.

00:12:26.800 --> 00:12:29.270
I repeat again, your mission is to observe.

00:12:29.270 --> 00:12:31.270
No engagement in battle. Okay?

00:12:31.310 --> 00:12:33.100
Roger.

00:12:34.600 --> 00:12:36.360
Patrol helicopter, taking off.

00:12:37.310 --> 00:12:39.900
Beartrap, to returning rail.

00:12:49.790 --> 00:12:52.540
Beartrap. Arrival at the returning rail!

00:12:52.540 --> 00:12:54.830
Crewmen on deck, stand by!

00:12:57.080 --> 00:12:59.500
Wing expansion, engine start.

00:13:10.760 --> 00:13:12.520
Beartrap open!

00:13:12.930 --> 00:13:14.440
Take off!

00:13:43.010 --> 00:13:45.220
Fortune Inspector, Sea Fowl.

00:13:45.220 --> 00:13:48.430
Take off complete. Skyline clear.

00:13:52.010 --> 00:13:55.430
My grandfather is 72 years old.

00:13:55.430 --> 00:13:57.850
He was born in Ogasawara.

00:13:58.600 --> 00:14:02.440
He's evacuated to the mainland in 1944,

00:14:02.440 --> 00:14:04.940
before the American Force attacks got intense.

00:14:04.990 --> 00:14:06.360
So...

00:14:06.860 --> 00:14:08.700
It's a weird feeling.

00:14:08.700 --> 00:14:10.990
Since it's the Showa 17th year,

00:14:11.080 --> 00:14:14.540
my grandfather should still be a school kid, in Chichijima's Ogura,

00:14:14.540 --> 00:14:16.960
playing with his friends with snot in his nose!

00:14:17.000 --> 00:14:19.960
Sea Fowl! Twenty minutes to Chichijima.

00:14:20.250 --> 00:14:21.540
Captain,

00:14:21.540 --> 00:14:24.250
even though it's a HS-Link transmission,

00:14:24.250 --> 00:14:25.170
it's still too risky.

00:14:25.550 --> 00:14:27.670
I'm prepared to take the risk.

00:14:27.670 --> 00:14:29.680
The decision to enter Yokosuka Base or not,

00:14:29.680 --> 00:14:32.050
lies with this observation expedition.

00:14:32.390 --> 00:14:36.230
Let us witness the actual situation with our eyes,

00:14:36.850 --> 00:14:39.560
before we make further decisions.

00:14:40.560 --> 00:14:44.020
Sea Fowl to Fortune Inspector. Target in sight.

00:14:44.020 --> 00:14:48.610
10 minutes to arrival. Cloud density 2, visibility clear.

00:14:52.200 --> 00:14:54.030
Oh, it's Ogasawara!

00:14:54.030 --> 00:14:56.700
Looking at it now, it's not much different from the present.

00:15:14.560 --> 00:15:17.470
In the exciting story known as history,

00:15:17.470 --> 00:15:19.850
this country has a shining legacy.

00:15:19.850 --> 00:15:21.940
Right now, the ones who know about this...

00:15:21.940 --> 00:15:25.230
...are the 241 crew members on this ship and myself.

00:15:27.230 --> 00:15:29.110
Is there a purpose for this?

00:15:31.910 --> 00:15:34.580
I see Futami Port, Chichijima!

00:15:34.580 --> 00:15:37.200
Current altitude, 2800 feet.

00:15:37.200 --> 00:15:40.000
We'll descend to 500 feet from now on.

00:15:40.080 --> 00:15:41.580
500's too dangerous!

00:15:41.580 --> 00:15:44.630
- You know I can handle this.
- I believe in you.

00:15:44.630 --> 00:15:47.800
I wouldn't have opted to be your gunner if I didn't. However...

00:15:47.880 --> 00:15:51.720
However...? You can let the pigs eat your conditional trust!

00:15:51.970 --> 00:15:53.340
Let's go.

00:15:56.010 --> 00:15:59.140
Sea Fowl, we'll be approaching the bay now.

00:15:59.270 --> 00:16:01.560
There's something on the right side of the bay.

00:16:01.560 --> 00:16:03.770
Is it a ship, or another plane? Can you make sure?

00:16:04.400 --> 00:16:06.570
Wait a minute. Let me verify.

00:16:07.020 --> 00:16:10.490
I see them! There are two supply ships parked in the port.

00:16:10.490 --> 00:16:12.400
And right behind them...

00:16:12.610 --> 00:16:14.110
...are two spy planes!

00:16:14.910 --> 00:16:16.740
That's dangerous! If we're spotted by them...!

00:16:16.740 --> 00:16:18.700
Please hurry and escape now!

00:16:18.830 --> 00:16:21.210
Near the coast, there appears to be a barrack of some sort,

00:16:21.210 --> 00:16:23.750
and village houses without antennas attached.

00:16:23.870 --> 00:16:25.670
Numerous transportation vessels sighted.

00:16:25.670 --> 00:16:28.460
No mistake about it. It is the Showa 17th year!

00:16:28.750 --> 00:16:30.260
We're drifters!

00:16:30.260 --> 00:16:33.470
We can never go back to our families ever again!

00:16:37.800 --> 00:16:41.680
So we won't be able to go back to Japan until this war is over, right?

00:16:41.680 --> 00:16:43.730
That'll be in 3 years and 2 months.

00:16:43.730 --> 00:16:46.520
To be drifting in the Pacific Ocean for that long...

00:16:46.520 --> 00:16:49.320
It's just not possible! We are living people.

00:16:49.320 --> 00:16:51.240
We all need to breathe and eat!

00:16:51.400 --> 00:16:54.110
Let's go back to Yokosuka! Let's go back to Japan again!

00:16:54.110 --> 00:16:57.570
It doesn't matter if the soldiers capture or interrogate us.

00:16:57.570 --> 00:17:00.740
They're all Japanese, too. They will understand us!

00:17:00.740 --> 00:17:04.370
And if they want us to aid them in this war, then we should do so!

00:17:04.370 --> 00:17:07.750
It's much better than being chased around this Pacific Ocean!

00:17:07.750 --> 00:17:09.380
That's right! That's a better idea!

00:17:09.380 --> 00:17:10.880
No way!

00:17:10.880 --> 00:17:14.340
If we were to do that, they will want to take our ship away.

00:17:14.590 --> 00:17:16.930
What's more, all our crew members will be separated.

00:17:16.930 --> 00:17:19.930
This Mirai is the only country we have left!

00:17:19.930 --> 00:17:22.720
How can we hand this country of ours over just like that?!

00:17:22.720 --> 00:17:26.230
But, Exec! What about our food and our fuel supplies?!

00:17:26.230 --> 00:17:28.360
If we can't move anymore, we will hide instead.

00:17:28.360 --> 00:17:30.020
To prevent the alteration of history,

00:17:30.020 --> 00:17:31.650
and the handing over of this ship,

00:17:31.650 --> 00:17:33.240
this is the only way left for us.

00:17:33.240 --> 00:17:34.860
There's another way.

00:17:35.610 --> 00:17:37.990
- What?
- Getting supplies is possible.

00:17:37.990 --> 00:17:42.160
No one can live disguised as the dead.

00:17:42.160 --> 00:17:44.910
If all of you choose to continue living,

00:17:44.910 --> 00:17:46.870
I will do my best to help all of you.

00:17:46.870 --> 00:17:50.250
Is that a form of gratitude? I'll be glad to accept it.

00:17:50.250 --> 00:17:53.050
I heard that this ship runs on diesel.

00:17:53.050 --> 00:17:55.170
We should find some gas in the South Pacific.

00:17:55.220 --> 00:17:57.300
We can find something like that? Where?

00:17:57.340 --> 00:18:00.390
The former dutch colony, Asia's largest oil producer,

00:18:00.390 --> 00:18:02.760
- Palembang.
- Palembang?

00:18:02.760 --> 00:18:05.430
In the largest city of North-eastern Sumatra,

00:18:05.430 --> 00:18:09.810
which is occupied by Japan since the 14th of February this year.

00:18:09.810 --> 00:18:13.480
There's inexhaustible crude oil, and 2 oil refineries there.

00:18:13.570 --> 00:18:15.690
If you don't wish to give up this ship,

00:18:15.690 --> 00:18:18.110
refueling is the only way left for you to go.

00:18:24.410 --> 00:18:26.460
Direction 7 o'clock! Distance 1500!

00:18:26.460 --> 00:18:28.870
Two vessels approaching! Speed, 230!

00:18:28.870 --> 00:18:30.580
It's way too fast for spy planes!

00:18:30.580 --> 00:18:32.210
230?!

00:18:35.710 --> 00:18:38.180
Those aren't ordinary spy planes!

00:18:38.180 --> 00:18:40.090
Target closing in rapidly!

00:18:40.090 --> 00:18:42.470
Fast approaching our maximum speed!

00:18:44.310 --> 00:18:47.680
Emergency! Two Japanese planes closing in!

00:18:47.680 --> 00:18:49.140
Oh, no! Sea Fowl!

00:18:49.140 --> 00:18:51.650
Abandon mission and retreat immediately!

00:18:51.650 --> 00:18:54.020
Roger! Retreating immediately!

00:18:54.110 --> 00:18:56.070
Hey, look! There are two planes pursuing them!

00:18:56.070 --> 00:18:57.900
Watch out! Shake them off and get out of there!

00:18:57.900 --> 00:19:00.110
Prepare for Anti-Air Warfare!

00:19:04.030 --> 00:19:05.580
Fascinating.

00:19:05.580 --> 00:19:07.700
Even an expedition from such a long distance...

00:19:07.700 --> 00:19:10.330
...can be viewed through images of such clarity.

00:19:10.620 --> 00:19:12.540
If our Navy fleet had this,

00:19:12.540 --> 00:19:15.420
we could've sunk the US carriers at Midway.

00:19:15.500 --> 00:19:18.300
Lieutenant Kusaka, what're those spy planes armed with?

00:19:18.670 --> 00:19:21.680
Spy planes? Those aren't spy planes.

00:19:21.720 --> 00:19:24.470
- What?!
- Those are Type 2 sea planes.

00:19:24.470 --> 00:19:28.520
Each armed with two 20mm and 7.7 mm machineguns.

00:19:32.190 --> 00:19:34.230
No matter what the circumstances are,

00:19:34.230 --> 00:19:36.980
we must never try to run away from it all.

00:19:36.980 --> 00:19:40.200
The one who taught me this, is you.

00:19:44.740 --> 00:19:48.160
Why are you moving the wings about like this, Lieutenant Satake?

00:19:48.250 --> 00:19:49.540
It's known as banking.

00:19:49.540 --> 00:19:52.080
It's supposed to be a signal of friendship in their time.

00:19:52.080 --> 00:19:54.210
I'm not sure if it still holds true though.

00:19:59.170 --> 00:20:00.840
I can see the Red Sun, but...

00:20:00.840 --> 00:20:03.390
The Imperial Navy doesn't have a "Self Defense Force".

00:20:03.390 --> 00:20:05.390
They give the bank signal, yet they run away!

00:20:05.510 --> 00:20:07.350
What's taking you so long?!

00:20:07.350 --> 00:20:09.220
Are you gonna just watch the Umidori get destroyed?!

00:20:09.310 --> 00:20:11.730
According to Yanagi, those aren't spy planes!

00:20:11.730 --> 00:20:13.770
They're Type 2 sea planes, with floats attached!

00:20:13.810 --> 00:20:14.860
...Fighter planes.

00:20:14.900 --> 00:20:17.940
Well, if you know that, then give permission to fire!

00:20:18.110 --> 00:20:20.530
If Satake doesn't do anything about them now...

00:20:20.530 --> 00:20:21.900
...they won't be able to return.

00:20:21.990 --> 00:20:24.610
Otherwise, they'll guide the fighter planes back to Mirai.

00:20:24.700 --> 00:20:25.740
I know that.

00:20:25.820 --> 00:20:27.490
Well then, since they've been spotted...!

00:20:27.490 --> 00:20:29.580
We only have the choice of shooting them down!

00:20:29.750 --> 00:20:30.790
Oguri.

00:20:30.870 --> 00:20:32.370
Permission to fire not granted.

00:20:32.580 --> 00:20:36.380
Kikuchi! If Satake's killed then it's your damn fault!

00:20:37.460 --> 00:20:40.920
Executive Officer, contact the Umidori one more time.

00:20:40.920 --> 00:20:41.880
Roger.

00:20:42.130 --> 00:20:45.090
Lieutenant Satake! Never mind if this ship is discovered.

00:20:45.090 --> 00:20:47.010
Come back at once!

00:20:47.010 --> 00:20:49.430
We'll do something if they follow you back.

00:20:49.430 --> 00:20:51.270
I'll bear the responsibility.

00:20:51.390 --> 00:20:52.770
One of the interceptor planes...

00:20:52.890 --> 00:20:56.060
...has resumed firing position. It's critical.

00:20:56.060 --> 00:20:58.110
To refrain from initiating battle,

00:20:58.110 --> 00:21:00.650
it's a rule we must keep for as long as possible.

00:21:00.650 --> 00:21:01.860
There's no need for battle...

00:21:01.940 --> 00:21:04.110
...in a disadvantageous position. Come back now!

00:21:04.320 --> 00:21:06.910
This is an order, Lieutenant Satake!

00:21:06.910 --> 00:21:09.450
Battle initiation forbidden.

00:21:09.450 --> 00:21:12.370
We've had that rule since the force was formed.

00:21:12.370 --> 00:21:14.120
I'm used to it.

00:21:14.580 --> 00:21:17.000
It's my fault we've been spotted.

00:21:17.000 --> 00:21:18.840
I'll definitely shake them off!

00:21:20.960 --> 00:21:23.510
- It's moving!
- It'll fire from the back!

00:21:23.510 --> 00:21:24.760
Left turn!

00:21:30.680 --> 00:21:32.470
It has started! Right turn!

00:21:32.470 --> 00:21:34.350
- We're hitting the surface!
- Got it!

00:21:36.770 --> 00:21:39.310
The other plane is nowhere in sight! I've lost sight of it!

00:21:39.310 --> 00:21:40.270
It's on top!

00:21:44.780 --> 00:21:46.610
You're not bad.

00:21:46.700 --> 00:21:48.070
Checking state of damage.

00:21:48.070 --> 00:21:50.780
Electric component, navigation system in working order.

00:21:50.780 --> 00:21:54.040
Fuel tank intact. Damage isn't serious! Just some scratches!

00:21:54.040 --> 00:21:56.370
Mori! It's our turn next...

00:21:56.410 --> 00:21:57.830
Mori...?!

00:22:00.250 --> 00:22:04.130
Mori...!!

00:22:09.720 --> 00:22:17.270
Passing through the distant time

00:22:17.400 --> 00:22:22.480
Just peacefully

00:22:21.970 --> 00:22:34.290
Without losing your way, you walked towards me

00:22:35.420 --> 00:22:47.170
How many times have I grasped tightly those small hands of yours?

00:22:47.670 --> 00:22:53.810
Not being able to do anything

00:22:54.370 --> 00:22:59.880
I kept on praying

00:23:01.250 --> 00:23:11.690
Sorrow or agony isn't enough

00:23:13.560 --> 00:23:27.370
That's why now as if I wanted to make up... I'm looking at you

00:23:40.760 --> 00:23:42.390
Satake, I know you're capable of this.

00:23:42.680 --> 00:23:43.930
I trust your skills.

00:23:44.140 --> 00:23:46.520
On the battlefield, when life and death are next to each other,

00:23:46.520 --> 00:23:48.560
there is no guarantee of one's existence tomorrow.

00:23:48.560 --> 00:23:50.560
Neither for me, or for this ship.

00:23:50.560 --> 00:23:52.440
The peace that we are so proud of now,

00:23:52.440 --> 00:23:54.730
is not something that's maintained solely by guns and weapons!

00:23:54.730 --> 00:23:56.940
The opponents are Japanese, too!

00:23:57.030 --> 00:23:59.450
Is there a need for us to be killing our own people?!

00:24:00.040 --> 00:24:04.960
Next Episode: Order For Attack

00:24:00.110 --> 00:24:01.910
Welcome to this era.

00:24:02.070 --> 00:24:04.120
Starting from now, you are the guest.

00:24:04.960 --> 00:24:09.960
This story is purely fiction. The names of the
characters and organizations that appear have no
connections with actual people and organizations.
